This is going to a little tricky. `OperationTypeCoder` needs to import an "external" type, i.e. `script.importExternalType()`. 

But it doesn't know the path of that external type, because it depends on which directories have a `_.context.ts` file. And the way the code works now, `Script` doesn't know the directories where the files will be written, so it can't check.

I'm thinking about adding an `importContextType()` method to Script. Each `Script` is constructed in `Repository`. Currently, `Repository` doesn't know where the files are written either until `writeFiles(destination)` is called. What we can do then is have `importContextType()` use a placeholder token for the path. Then when `Repository#writeFiles(destination)` is called it can determine where the `_.context.ts` file is and replace the token.

Okay, so the first thing to do is add a function to Repository:

```ts
function findContextPath(destination, path) {
   // return the relative path to the best-match _.context.ts file
}
```

Then we can replace the token. And all that's left is to create the token in the first place, which is trivial.

