```

The first step I think is to refactor so that we pass the source directory as the first argument to ModuleLoader, and have ModuleLoader create the Transpiler. That would make `compiledPathsDirectory` (i.e. the `.cache` directory) an implementation detail of ModuleLoader.

`determineModuleKind()` can also get stuffed inside of `ModuleLoader`.

Then we can factor out an `uncachedImport()` function with one of two implementations, depending on the module kind:

- `uncached-import.js` uses `import()` and attaches a random querystring to the end of the module name.
- `uncached-import.cjs` uses `require()` after deleting the `require.cache` entry.

That also paves the way for eventually getting rid of the `.cache` directory and using a VM.

